            <ArticleTitle>Making connections: integration of psychiatric and medical-surgical nursing and relationship-based care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a growing recognition of mind-body connection in our culture. Relationship-based care (RBC) represents a theoretical foundation for the application of the mind-body connection in the clinical setting. This article describes ways to incorporate mind-body and RBC concepts into nursing classroom and clinical experiences.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
